The question's solution depends on whether the robot pattern ever hits a wall. If the robot halts after a certain number of moves, this ensures that different cells are never hit more than once. Yet, if the pattern is non-repeating, the robot never hits a wall hencely it will "eternalily" move on after first hit, leading to an infinite loop. Thus, the class of cases is given by the robot pattern as follows: the resulting sequence is cyclic non-repeating (or coincides arbitrarily with pattern rotation).

A simple validation for non-repeating pattern would be done by also ensuring the condition that no more than one usage of a pattern exists per a row, per a column and also of the total number of items being used. Let's proceed with the Python solution:

